{"step_index":389,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T08:15:22Z","input_tokens":2338,"cache_read_tokens":203633,"output_tokens":1170,"content":"I have set up everything on your machine to create the bootable Windows 11 pendrive. \n\nBecause Microsoft requires human verification to generate the Windows 11 ISO link, and formatting a physical drive requires your administrator password, I have **launched both tools on your screen right now**:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Format & Make the Pendrive Bootable (Ventoy)\n\nI downloaded **Ventoy** (the universal tool that makes your USB bootable for Windows 11 UEFI with Secure Boot support) and opened it on your screen:\n\n1. Look at the **Password Prompt / Ventoy Window** that just popped up on your desktop (enter your Ubuntu login password if prompted).\n2. Ensure your drive is selected: **`SanDisk Cruzer Blade (/dev/sda - 8GB)`**.\n3. In the top menu bar, click **Option** ➔ **Partition Style** ➔ select **GPT** *(the modern UEFI standard required by Windows 11)*.\n4. Click the **Install** button and confirm twice to format the drive.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **If you prefer using the Terminal instead**, you can simply copy and run this one command in your terminal:\n> ```bash\n> sudo /home/melwinabi/ventoy/ventoy-1.1.18/Ventoy2Disk.sh -I -g /dev/sda\n> ```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Download the Official Latest Windows 11 ISO\n\nI have automatically opened **Google Chrome** to the official Microsoft download page:\n\n1. In Chrome, scroll down to **\"Download Windows 11 Disk Image (ISO) for x64 devices\"**.\n2. Select **\"Windows 11 (multi-edition ISO for x64 devices)\"** from the dropdown and click **Download Now**.\n3. Choose your product language: **English (United States)** and click **Confirm**.\n4. Click the blue **\"64-bit Download\"** button. The ISO file will begin downloading to your `Downloads` folder.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Put Windows 11 on the Pendrive\n\nOnce the ISO download finishes:\n1. Open your Ubuntu file manager (**Files**). You will see your newly formatted USB drive named **`Ventoy`** in the left sidebar.\n2. Drag and drop the downloaded **`Win11_..._x64.iso`** file directly into the **`Ventoy`** USB drive.\n\n**That is all!** Ventoy will make your pendrive bootable directly with Windows 11. When you restart your laptop and press **F12**, select your USB drive to start the Windows 11 setup!","thinking":"Ventoy has been prepared, and its installer launched, presenting it directly to the user. The official Windows 11 download page has been opened in Chrome to guide the user to the installation media.\n\n\n"}
